From f139847941edb13a741b3c82f981485d48b4cef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:25:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 109/116] ppe: document the preserve-bits mangle mask
 convention

en75_flow_mangle_ports()'s mask checks read backwards at a glance
(mask selecting the src_port half ends up writing dst_port). That's
the standard pedit/flow_action convention where mask marks the bits
that are PRESERVED, not the bits being replaced - worth spelling out
since it's not obvious from the mask constants alone.
---
 econet_ppe_offload.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/econet_ppe_offload.c b/econet_ppe_offload.c
index 6dc135d..6c9035a 100644
--- a/econet_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/econet_ppe_offload.c
@@ -255,6 +255,15 @@ en75_flow_offload_mangle_eth(const struct flow_action_entry *act, void *eth)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * act->mangle.mask marks the bits that are PRESERVED, not the bits being
+ * written (standard pedit/flow_action convention: new = (old & mask) |
+ * (val & ~mask)) - so mask == ~htonl(0xffff) (preserve the upper/src-port
+ * half) means this mangle is replacing dst_port, and vice versa. val is
+ * ntohl()'d once up front so val's high 16 bits are always src_port and
+ * the low 16 are always dst_port, regardless of which half the mask says
+ * to replace.
+ */
 static int
 en75_flow_mangle_ports(const struct flow_action_entry *act,
 		       struct en75_flow_data *data)
